WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.170
While the R-Rated movie Logan — the third
film in the solo Wolverine franchise — isn't

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.900
set to drop until March 3, 2017, we have a
little taste of what's in store thanks to

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:10.910
the first trailer.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:15.130
It sure seems to be inspired by Marvel’s
Old Man Logan comic series, but just how much

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:18.040
can we expect Logan to borrow from these pages?

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.710
Here's what you might have missed in the Logan
trailer.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.199
No more mutants

00:00:22.199 --> 00:00:26.000
Logan was always a reluctant member of the
X-Men, but underneath it all, he may have

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.830
needed them more than they needed him.

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:31.830
When we see Logan drinking alone at the cemetery,
just who is he mourning for?

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:32.830
"Logan.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.140
What did you do?"

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:39.009
"Charles, the world is not the same as it
was.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.500
Mutants...they're gone now."

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:49.600
This hints that Logan might follow at least
one major plot point of the Old Man Logan

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.600
storyline.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:54.140
Believing the X-Mansion is under siege by
a group of villains, Wolverine takes them

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.750
on himself and kills them all.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:59.680
It's only after they're all dead that he realizes
he's been tricked, and that he's actually

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.039
killed the X-Men.

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:05.280
In anguish, he gives up the Wolverine persona
and waits to die in a world mostly devoid

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.310
of superheroes.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:09.290
It's obviously too soon to tell whether Logan
will follow the comics.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:14.049
But in a mature movie that promises to be
emotional, gritty, and takes death seriously,

00:01:14.049 --> 00:01:18.700
a scene depicting Wolverine's slaughter of
the X-Men would be unlike anything ever seen

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.640
in a superhero movie.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.040
X-23

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:26.119
In the trailer, our hero is introduced to
a young girl who seems to have a lot in common

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:27.330
with Wolverine himself...

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.600
"She's like you.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:31.740
Very much like you."

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:35.100
This is Laura Kinney, also known as X-23.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.910
In the comics, her powers are like Wolverine's.

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:40.280
She has retracting claws and she can rapidly
regenerate.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:44.210
So here's our question: will she be Logan’s
cloned daughter, like she is in the comics?

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:47.159
Or will he just feel a bond with her over
their shared abilities?

00:01:47.159 --> 00:01:51.409
The trailer implies that Logan is forced into
action when Laura is kidnapped, which is a

00:01:51.409 --> 00:01:53.950
complete departure from the Old Man Logan
series.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:57.799
Closer to the end of the trailer, Logan has
to extend his own hand-stabbers to protect

00:01:57.799 --> 00:01:59.650
himself against a claw-like attack.

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:03.680
Either Laura is demonstrating her fighting
skills to Logan to show him how they're alike…

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.509
or she’s being forced to fight him.

00:02:05.509 --> 00:02:07.979
Those are our best guesses, at least…

00:02:07.979 --> 00:02:09.560
Donald Pierce

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:14.129
The main villain of the film is a cyborg named
Donald Pierce, an anti-mutant fanatic with

00:02:14.129 --> 00:02:15.360
a cybernetic hand.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.810
In the comics, Pierce has a gang of fellow
cyborgs, the Reavers, and they go around hunting

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:20.900
down mutants.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:25.120
They have a specific hatred for Wolverine,
because the Reavers became cyborgs after he

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.459
chopped off their limbs.

00:02:26.459 --> 00:02:30.040
To be fair, most people would be at least
a little put out about that too.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.599
"Tis but a scratch!"

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:32.599
"A scratch?!

00:02:32.599 --> 00:02:33.599
Your arm's off!"

00:02:33.599 --> 00:02:34.099
"No it isn't!"

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.700
The Reavers have been confirmed for Logan,
and it appears that they’ll act like a private

00:02:37.709 --> 00:02:39.980
security force that works under Pierce.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:43.730
It also seems like Pierce and the Reavers
have some official backing, because they use

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:48.520
the South American Federal Police to go after
Logan, Laura, and Charles.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.980
Professor X

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:54.220
One big question about the Logan trailer is
why Pierce seems to kidnap Laura and leave

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:57.140
Logan alive after having him surrounded and
restrained?

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:00.580
This suggests there could be a much more complex
plot at the heart of Logan.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.120
What if Pierce's real target is Charles Xavier?

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.420
In the comics, Pierce captures Charles and
tries to harness his power to hunt mutants,

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:10.780
so it’s possible that this will also be
a plot point in Logan.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:15.030
Uncoincidentally, the mutant Caliban also
figures into Logan, who also has the power

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.440
to track other mutants.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:20.170
We also see a scene showing guns pointed at
Charles' head while he’s clearly using his

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.590
mental powers as Laura crawls towards him.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:26.470
What if Charles was too difficult to kidnap,
so the bad guys took Laura hostage instead?

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:30.739
That seems like a convoluted plot, but it
would add an emotional Sophie's Choice element

00:03:30.739 --> 00:03:33.730
to a film in which the main character wants
to die.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.310
Funeral for a friend

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:40.040
Presuming Logan did kill all the X-Men, Charles
Xavier was probably able to avoid being killed

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.450
because of his abilities.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:45.239
As to why Charles didn't stop the massacre
has yet to be seen, but it appears that out

00:03:45.239 --> 00:03:49.380
of everyone from Logan’s old life, the only
mutant, or living thing, that Logan cares

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:50.569
for is Charles.

00:03:50.569 --> 00:03:54.299
At the end of the trailer, we see Wolverine
covered in blood and looking mournfully at

00:03:54.299 --> 00:03:56.180
the ground while holding a shovel.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:59.950
Logan has killed a lot of people in his day,
but he's rarely taken the time to personally

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.019
bury anyone.

00:04:01.019 --> 00:04:03.700
You get one guess about who's taking the dirt
nap…

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.080
Thanks for watching!

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:08.379
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:11.770
And leave us a comment to let us know what
has you most excited about Logan...

